  "title": "Emergence under the source-aware reading depends on the law (entropy) and on the world (frozen or flexible)",
  "subject": "Which laws and which worlds have native loops and native knots",
  "conclusion": "Under the source-aware reading emergence depends on the law and the world: a linear law has native knots at every world or at none (on Z^d exactly when it has positive entropy; Ledrappier's law and Tseitin plus gauge are frozen), while proper 3-colourings have frozen worlds where the star knot 'not all distinct' is not native and dense flexible worlds where it is. Native loops are not sufficient: the hard-core law is flexible everywhere but has no knot.",
